+- Open: [a residency commit does not return on an iPad](../../../docs/reference/rendering.md#a-residency-commit-does-not-return-on-an-ipad). A device stackshot identifies the replay thread's driver call and the guest main thread waiting behind it. Opt-in residency and teardown checkpoints gather the next failure, without changing rendering or claiming a fix.
+
 - [GPU frame captures need pipelines built through the device](../../../docs/reference/shaders.md#gpu-frame-captures-need-pipelines-built-through-the-device): fixed for every game ([PR #2688](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2688)). An M1 session with `MTL_CAPTURE_ENABLED=0` left set ran without the Metal 4 pipelines: `hybrid pipelines off`, 467 pipeline stalls of about 170 ms and one 84 s freeze. The host now asks Metal whether the run can capture.
 - [A scene that does not fit the shorter hold probed against another scene's GPU time](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#a-scene-that-does-not-fit-the-shorter-hold-probed-against-another-scenes-gpu-time): fixed in the frame step for every game. Hyrule Field at night on an M2 Pro (22 failed probes a minute, 159 frames at 20 fps, PR [#2611](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2611)) and Kokiri Forest at each turn of the camera on an Android port. On an M4 Pro at render scale 1.333, standing at the Hyrule Field save point: 9 and 13 failed probes a run before, 2 after; the M2 Pro retest is open.
 - [A frame's submissions queued behind its first one while the iPhone's GPU clock is low](../../../docs/reference/frame-rate.md#a-frames-submissions-queued-behind-its-first-one-while-the-iphones-gpu-clock-is-low): the stalls resolved by holding the submissions that end behind running work and committing them together, each in its own command buffer ([PR #2645](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2645)); the low clock itself open. On the iPhone 17 at the 30 fps cap (2026-11-14) the game fell to 5-10 fps in Hyrule Field and Kakariko Village by night and to 12 fps in a fairy fountain (640 draws), also after a restart, for no more work than by day. With the fix (the owner's play, about 30 minutes): about 17 fps in those places by night against about 9, 30 fps in most of the rest (frame p50 33.3 ms, `GPU p50` 29-30 ms), and none of the first version's pink and dark flashes or GPU errors. The slow windows left are no longer GPU-bound (`GPU p50` 13-20 ms, the submit thread 11-24 ms at 1.3-1.7 GHz, pipeline bases compiling in the background): separate work, open. That session ended in a memory kill (`JetsamEvent`, the app at 4.2 GB) at the village's entrance to the castle grounds, in a frame that loaded 301 new textures (204 MB): not attributed, open. On the M6 (2026-11-15, `save_village` with the encode thread on, two runs a side against main `f226affd`): `NVN submit+present` p50 3.2-3.4 ms against 4.1-5.5 ms, `GPU p50` and the locked 60 fps unchanged, no `[RED]` line. Open: this version's frame-by-frame numbers on the iPhone, and what releasing held work on the GPU's own event saves there (`DM_NVN_SUB_MERGE=ab:1,2/3 DM_NVN_SUB_IDLE_FB=ab:1/3 DM_AB=900`).
