+### A residency commit does not return on an iPad
+
+- **Symptom:** a black picture after preparation, sometimes only after returning to the library and starting again. Quitting may leave the process unable to finish exiting, and the next app launch stays black.
+- **Cause:** open. A Time Profiler initial stackshot on an M2 iPad Pro (iPadOS 27.0.1, 24A446) places the NVN replay thread in `IOGPUResourceGroupUpdateResources`, through `-[IOGPUMetalResidencySet commit]`, `res_commit`, `gmem_map` and `encode_args`. The guest main thread waits in `mtl_reg_tex` for `g_rmu`, held by that replay path. UIKit's main thread is in its run loop. This locates the wait, but does not explain why the driver has not returned. It also occurred on a first launch after reboot with `DM_GUEST_FILE_PUNCH=0`, so that switch is not a sufficient workaround. A similar residency wait is described in [PR #2098](https://github.com/seedds/nxnative/pull/2098) for another game and device, without establishing a shared cause.
+- **Fix:** none confirmed. `DM_RES_TRACE=1` adds synchronous, numbered checkpoints before the commit mutex, after acquiring it, around applying allocations, and around Metal's commit. Each batch records allocation counts and bytes and the submitted/completed fences. Large batches also name their eight largest added allocations, with shared buffer addresses but no buffer contents. `DM_TEARDOWN_TRACE=1` records the begin and end of every existing shell teardown step. Both are off by default, retain the existing synchronization and teardown order, and create no watchdog threads. A missing end checkpoint identifies the next wait to inspect, not a recovery action.
+- **Check:** `check_t_res_trace` gates a real residency set's commit and checks that the begin and batch lines can be read before the call returns, completion appears only afterwards, concurrent changes still queue, and actual residency is preserved, with tracing both on and off. `check_t_res_commit` exercises the existing serialization. Hardware diagnosis is ongoing and does not establish a fix or gameplay compatibility.
+- **Found on:** [The Legend of Zelda: Ocarina of Time](../../dm/games/0400486024DEC000/README.md#found-on-this-game), update v131072 in the personal iPad shell, engine `68179b6d470e`, shader chain `19d183a2b462`, 2026-11-18. The local experimental data set has three known damaged textures, whose relationship to this wait is unproven.
+
 ### Naming the shaders of a GPU fault
 
 - **Symptom:** `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorPageFault` or `kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang` on a command buffer, and nothing says which draw or dispatch caused it; `DM_RES_CHECK=1` reports no `missing residency`.
